functor: 1
title: arrow
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`arrow` · decorate · a vector.

# Form

`x.arrow` on a symbol, `(a + b).arrow` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `v.arrow` | $v.arrow$ | built and cached |
| `F.arrow` | $F.arrow$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A vector. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A mark above or below the base. The mark follows the slant of an italic letter. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\vec{v}` becomes `v.arrow`, but prefer `object vec: v`.

